<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Kisra (Borgu tradition)</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Kisra is a legendary conqueror in the traditions of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/borgu">Borgu</a>, in present-day <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/benin-empire">Benin</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nigeria">Nigeria</a>, said to have come from the east and to be the ancestor of the ruling dynasties of Bussa, Nikki and other Borgu kingdoms. Some scholars connect his name with Kisra, the Arabic form of the Persian royal name Khosrow. Similar origin stories are told among neighbouring peoples.</p></div>
